{"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"retry","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"E","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"_","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"retries","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Su","text":"UInt","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" = 1, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"on","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"error","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"E","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".Type) -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7Afluent14AsyncSequencesO","text":"AsyncSequences","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7Afluent14AsyncSequencesO11RetryOnCastC","text":"RetryOnCast","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences\/RetryOnCast"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"E","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7Afluent20RetryByCountStrategyC","text":"RetryByCountStrategy","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/RetryByCountStrategy"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"E","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s5ErrorP","text":"Error","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"name":"retries","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The maximum number of times to retry the upstream, defaulting to 1."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"error","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The specific error type that should trigger a retry if a cast succeeds.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Return Value","anchor":"return-value"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"An ","type":"text"},{"code":"AsyncSequence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" that emits the same output as the upstream but retries on the specified error up to the specified number of times.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This method returns an ","type":"text"},{"code":"AsyncSequence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" that retries the upstream only when an error can be cast to the specified error type, up to the given number of retries.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Not all "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsyncSequence"},{"type":"text","text":"s can be retried. For example, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsyncStream"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsyncThrowingStream"},{"type":"text","text":" cannot be retried on their own."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Example","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Example"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["actor CallCounter {","    private(set) var count = 0","    func increment() -> Int {","        count += 1","        return count","    }","}","","enum NetworkError: Error {","    case timeout","    case unknown","}","","let counter = CallCounter()","","let sequence = DeferredTask {","    let attempt = await counter.increment()","    if attempt < 2 {","        throw NetworkError.timeout","    }","    return 55","}",".toAsyncSequence()",".retry(3, on: NetworkError.self)","","for try await value in sequence {","    print(value) \/\/ prints 55 after retry on NetworkError.timeout","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"name":"Important","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Not every "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsyncSequence"},{"type":"text","text":" can be retried, for this to work the sequence has to implement an iterator that doesn’t preserve state across various creations."}]}],"type":"aside","style":"important"},{"name":"Note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"code":"AsyncStream","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"AsyncThrowingStream","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" are notable sequences which cannot be retried on their own."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside","style":"note"}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/afluent\/asyncsequences\/catch\/retry(_:on:)-9lony"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences\/Catch\/retry(_:on:)-9lony","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent","doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences","doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences\/Catch"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"Retries the upstream ","type":"text"},{"code":"AsyncSequence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" up to a specified number of times only when a specific error type is encountered.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"extendedModule":"_Concurrency","roleHeading":"Instance Method","symbolKind":"method","modules":[{"name":"Afluent","relatedModules":["_Concurrency"]}],"externalID":"s:Sci7Afluents8SendableRzsAB7ElementRpzrlE5retry_2onAA14AsyncSequencesO11RetryOnCastCy_xqd__AA0H15ByCountStrategyCGSu_qd__mts5ErrorRd__lF::SYNTHESIZED::s:7Afluent14AsyncSequencesO5CatchV","title":"retry(_:on:)","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Afluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Afluent\/SequenceOperators\/RetrySequence.swift#L481","fileName":"RetrySequence.swift"},"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"retry","kind":"id